					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-298875#post-2050954</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-298875/scp-193#post-2050954</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 13 Jun 2014 04:01:43 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Lumancer</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>662776</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Apologies if the phrasing is unclear. The line in question, modified to indicate my intent, would read:</p> <blockquote> <p>This [tendency to crawl back to the tissue box] continues in the presence of thoroughly insulated observers, but not in the presence of large artificial heat sources, supporting the theory that SCP-193-02 detects heat.</p> </blockquote> <p>Is that not how it comes across?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-298875#post-2044719</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-298875/scp-193#post-2044719</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 03 Jun 2014 12:48:44 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>thisguyhere</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1885146</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>It's mentioned in the entry that the tissues check for body heat to see if anyone is watching, and that they don't move if a person is in the room but that they do move if a large heat source is present. The entry says that this supports the theory that the tissues look for heat sources but I don't see how. If anything, I'd think it disproves the heat source theory as it seems that it has no problem with a non observing heat source but not a person. Unless of course the heat source needs to be a certain size to cause the effect&#8230; Explain please?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
